   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the county of Saratoga to discontinue for reforestation purposes the use of certain lands and to convey such lands",
    "basePrintNo": "S5901",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5901-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Saratoga County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5901\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing the county of Saratoga to discontinue for\nreforestation purposes the use of certain lands and to convey such\nlands\n\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the County of Saratoga to discontinue\nthe use of not greater that 9.013 acres of land for reforestation\npurposes that is identified in section 2 and to convey the same to the\nTown of Moreau in exchange for a new parcel identified in section 3\nthat shall be dedicated for reforestation purposes.\n\nSection 2 provides a legal description of the property to be conveyed.\n\nSection 3 provides a legal description of the property to be acquired\nby the County in exchange that shall be dedicated for reforestation\npurposes.\n\nSection 4 provides the bill shall be effective immediately.\n\nThe County Saratoga is willing to assist the Town of Moreau in regard\nto a proposed new court and public safety facility by conveying a\n9.013 acre parcel to the Town.\n\nHowever, the parcel in question has been dedicated for reforestation\npurposes and by virtue of Section 219 of the County Law, an act of the\nState Legislature is necessary in order to transfer the land.\n\nThe County as part of the agreement will replace the loss of\nreforestation land by obtaining from the Town another parcel of equal\nor greater fair market value to the lands being alienated which the\nCounty will dedicate for reforestation purposes.\n\nThe new parcel is adjacent to existing reforestation land already\nowned by the County, and is more suitable for reforestation purposes.\n\nThe land to be conveyed due to its location is ideally suited for\nlocating this public safety facility and is in the best interest of\nboth municipalities.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n06/24/08 S.8259-A Rules\n06/17/08 A.1164-A Local Governments\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the County of Saratoga.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
